<section class="section section-light">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px;">

    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Who We Are</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">A competitive circuit built for the Carolinas and Southern Virginia MCP community</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p>The Infinity Circuit is a regional competitive circuit for Marvel: Crisis Protocol, built to give players across the Carolinas and Southern Virginia a structured, season-long competitive experience with real stakes and a meaningful championship at the end of the season.</p>

      <p>We are not an official Atomic Mass Games product or program. We are players and organizers who wanted something more than one-off local events. The circuit gives players a reason to show up consistently, compete seriously, and build relationships with the regional community over the course of a full season.</p>

      <p>Every sanctioned event contributes to season standings. The best players earn invitations to the Infinity Gauntlet Championship. Six players can claim an Infinity Stone by winning a Qualifier outright. One player wins the Gauntlet.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-divider"></div>

    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">The Season</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">How it works</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p>Each season consists of a series of sanctioned <strong>Shards Events</strong> hosted by stores across the region, six <strong>Infinity Qualifiers</strong> at designated partner stores, and the <strong>Infinity Gauntlet Championship</strong>, an invitational event open only to qualified players.</p>

      <p>Players earn Shard Points at every sanctioned event based on placement and attendance. Your best four results count toward your season total, keeping the standings competitive for players who start late or cannot make every event.</p>

      <p>Win an Infinity Qualifier and you claim that event's Stone, guaranteeing a Championship invitation regardless of your Shard standing. The six Stone holders are joined by the top at-large Shard Point qualifiers to form the Championship field.</p>

      <p>Full rules are available on the <a href="/rules/">Rules page</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-divider"></div>

    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Organizers</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Built by the community, for the community</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p>The Infinity Circuit was founded by Will Hare and Chris Faulkenberry, two players who wanted to see a serious, well-run competitive circuit take root in the Carolinas and Southern Virginia region. What started as an idea between two friends only exists because of the stores, Tournament Organizers, and players who believed in it and showed up to make it real.</p>

      <p>Every TO who runs a sanctioned event, every store that opens its doors to the community, and every player who travels to compete is part of what makes the circuit work. The founders set the structure. The community fills it.</p>

